  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catalyzing Innovation for HIV Prevention in the Caribbean: A Multi-Country Grant for Equitable and Sustainable Access - Americas - Multicountry Caribbean CARICOM-PANCAP (01-Oct-2025-30-Sep-2028)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Caribbean CARICOM-PANCAP, HIV, Caribbean Community (CARICOM) (CARICOM)This program has the following goals: Accelerate the uptake of innovations, in service delivery and in addressing country-specific barriers, to improve access to HIV prevention and testing services for key populations in participant countries.. The objectives of this program are: Design, implement, and evaluate program innovations to overcome country-specific barriers and become sustainable options to enhance the availability, accessibility, affordability and quality of HIV prevention and testing services for and with key populations.  Strengthen national stewardship of HIV programs to respond to successful innovations in service delivery that increase the availability, accessibility, affordability and quality of HIV prevention and testing programs for key populations.</narrative>
  </description>
